title: "AI Reliability as Systems Architecture"

authors:
  - family-names: "Lai"
    given-names: "Johnny"

version: "1.0"

date-released: "2026-11-09"

abstract: >-
  AI reliability is a property of the complete AI-enabled system,
  not primarily of the AI model. This whitepaper presents an AI
  Reliability Architecture Framework for designing reliable AI-enabled
  systems as AI moves from generating information to participating in
  workflows, influencing decisions, and executing actions. The framework
  defines nine core components: Application Characteristics, Intended
  Operating Envelope, Reliability Profile, Reliability Domains,
  Reliability Requirements, Reliability Functions, Architectural Controls,
  Reliability Evidence, and Reliability Acceptance Criteria. Reliability
  Maintenance operates across the lifecycle. The paper also defines three
  supervisory Reliability Functions—Observe, Constrain, and Recover—and
  explains how authority, operating conditions, controls, evidence, human
  oversight, and security contribute to acceptable system operation.

